body:
Jira Link: [DB-3095](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-3095)
### Description

IN query does not return the right values when one element in the search key exceeds the numerical limit in a range split table.

Example: 
```
CREATE TABLE test (key smallint, val int, PRIMARY KEY(key ASC));
INSERT INTO test VALUES (1, 1);
INSERT INTO test VALUES (6, 6);
INSERT INTO test VALUES (11, 11);
INSERT INTO test VALUES (16, 16);

yugabyte=# SELECT * from test;
 key | val
-----+-----
   1 |   1
   6 |   6
  11 |  11
  16 |  16
(4 rows)

yugabyte=# SELECT * FROM test WHERE key in (1, 6);
 key | value
-----+-------
   1 |     1
   6 |     6
(2 rows)

yugabyte=# SELECT * FROM test WHERE key IN (1, 6::bigint);
 key | value
-----+-------
   1 |     1
   6 |     6
(2 rows)

-- WRONG RESULT
yugabyte=# SELECT * FROM test WHERE key IN (1, 40000);
 key | value
-----+-------
(0 rows)

yugabyte=# SELECT * FROM test WHERE where key IN (1, 4000000);
 key | value
-----+-------
   1 |     1
(1 row)

-- WRONG RESULT
yugabyte=# SELECT * FROM test WHERE where key IN (1, 6, 40000);
 key | value
-----+-------
(0 rows)

yugabyte=# SELECT * FROM test WHERE where key IN (1, 6, 400000);
 key | value
-----+-------
   1 |     1
   6 |     6
(2 rows)

```

The docDB RPC that is sent for the following request  `SELECT * FROM test WHERE where key IN (1, 6, 40000);`
is as follows 

```
"I0801 09":"24":"49.351615 183961088 pg_session.cc":213
]"Applying operation":{
   "READ active":"1 read_time":{
      "read":"<invalid> local_limit":"<invalid> global_limit":"<invalid> in_txn_limit":"<invalid> serial_no":0
   }"request":"client":"YQL_CLIENT_PGSQL stmt_id":"4451389536 schema_version":0 targets{
      "column_id":0
   }"targets"{
      "column_id":1
   }"targets"{
      "column_id":-8
   }"column_refs"{
      "ids":"0 ids":1
   }"is_forward_scan":"1 is_aggregate":"0 limit":"1024 return_paging_state":"1 ysql_catalog_version":"4 table_id":"000033e100003000800000000000400d""condition_expr"{
      "condition"{
         "op":"QL_OP_AND operands"{
            "condition"{
               "op":"QL_OP_IN operands"{
                  "column_id":0
               }"operands"{
                  "value"{
                     "list_value"{
                        "elems"{
                           "int16_value":1
                        }"elems"{
                           "int16_value":6
                        }"elems"{
                           "int16_value":-25536
                        }
                     }
                  }
               }
            }
         }
      }
   }"upper_bound"{
      "key":"487FFF9C407E21""is_inclusive":1
   }"col_refs"{
      "column_id":"0 attno":1
   }"col_refs"{
      "column_id":"1 attno":2
   }"partition_key":"488000000121"
}
```

We can see that the value list for 40000 is -25536, which is the overflown value. There are two issues here.
1. We could avoid pushing it to docDB --> [Issue 22974](https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/12974) is fixing that. But that works for only inequalities. Elements in a search array are part of equality conditions. Hence we have to deal with that in a different manner.
